! WHERE AN INTERRUPTION RAISED BY A BOX-HELD MULTIPLY LANDS, 2026-11-20
! (docs/microarchitecture_plan.md §1c step 5f, the level release and the
! interruption recovery; StretchCore's rl_int_recover).
!
! THE PAGES.  Ref. Manual printed p.48 (PDF 51): an interruption is taken
! "at the end of the operation during which the indicator is turned on",
! "before execution of the next instruction".  The 7030 runs the I-box
! ahead of the E-box but UNDOES that advance on an interruption: Perf.
! Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-24 (PDF 42), "All changes in the index
! registers and/or index indicators due to the advance processing by the
! I-box must now be undone", "The correct instruction counter value is
! also shipped back to the I-box", "The interruption action is quite
! similar to branch recovery"; Buchholz §15.6 (printed pp.246-247).  So on
! the real machine the interruption lands IMMEDIATELY after the multiply.
!
! THE MODEL, since 2026-11-20, recovers (rl_int_recover): it cancels the
! younger levels, restores the index words and index indicators the I-box
! changed after the multiply's level was loaded, and returns the counter
! to the instruction after the multiply.  The interruption instruction
! (entry 33, ZM, mask bit 12.33) is "SIC, WHERE" prefixed to "B, DONE"
! (printed p.49's table form), which stores the instruction counter the
! interruption left (p.48: it points at the instruction displaced) and
! skips the LVIs not yet run.  ZM comes on for a zero product with
! exponent 0 (fp_zm_cleared's operands).
!   CASE 1: L, *, then four LVIs -- the I-box runs ahead as usual.
!   CASE 2: an LX held behind an earlier ST level keeps the I-box back
!           until the multiply is about to reach the box, then four LVIs.
! The LVIs are the trail: each sets one index register (X6-X9, X10-X14),
! so what committed before the interruption is seen, not only the
! counter.
! The printed answer, for both, is the instruction right after the
! multiply, with no LVI run: 4234 in case 1 and 4249 in case 2 -- the LX
! held behind the ST, which shares the multiply's word.  (This header
! said 4250, "the first LVI after the held LX", until 2026-11-20; the LX
! is AFTER the multiply, so p.48's "before execution of the next
! instruction" gives 4249.  Its X3 is 0 either way, so case 2 shows the
! LX's undoing in the counter only.)  The model now gives both; before
! the recovery it gave 4236 with X6, X7 set and 4251 with X10 set.  The
! run line in tests/run_tests.sh has the injections.
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable while IA and the mask are set
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        BBZ, $ZM,  $+1.0
        BB1, 12.33, $+1.0            ! ZM's mask bit := ONE
        BE,  $+.32                   ! ENABLE
! CASE 1: the multiply straight from the program.
        L(U), ZF0
        *(N), NZF0                   ! ZM on: the interruption
TRL1    LVI, $X6, 1                  ! the trail: each sets one index
        LVI, $X7, 1                  !   register, so what committed
        LVI, $X8, 1                  !   before the interruption is seen
        LVI, $X9, 1
DONE    BD,  $+.32                   ! entry 33 branches here
        BB,  CASEF+.0, FIN           ! case 2 done: finish
        LX,  $X5, WHERE              ! keep case 1's counter
        SX,  $X5, WHERE1
        BB1, CASEF+.0, $+1.0
        BE,  $+.32
! CASE 2: the I-box held back until the multiply is about to reach the box.
        L(U), ZF0
        ST(U), TMP                   ! a level storing TMP ...
        *(N), NZF0                   ! ZM on: the interruption
        LX,  $X3, TMP                ! ... holds this LX until it is gone
TRL2    LVI, $X10, 1
        LVI, $X11, 1
        LVI, $X12, 1
        LVI, $X14, 1
        B,   DONE
FIN     B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)6300.0
ZF0     DD(BU,64), 0                 ! fraction 0, exponent 0
NZF0    DD(BU,64), 2251799813685248  ! fraction 2**47, exponent 0
        SLC, (8)6400.0
WHERE   DD, 0                        ! the counter the interruption left
WHERE1  DD, 0                        ! ... in case 1
CASEF   DD, 0
TMP     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)6500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)6541.0
ZMRTN   SIC, WHERE                   ! entry 33 = ZM: SIC prefixed to a
        B,   DONE                    !   branch (p.49's SIC,X / B form)
        END, START
